 "prompt": "Model a shaft support assembly of four positioned parts (all dimensions in mm, one common coordinate system).\nbuild() must return a dict with exactly these keys: \"base_plate\", \"housing_left\", \"housing_right\", \"shaft\" \u2014 each value a cadquery Workplane holding one solid, already in its assembled position.\n- base_plate: 160 along X, 60 along Y, 10 thick, centred on the origin in X and Y, Z from 0 to 10.\n- housing_left / housing_right: blocks 20 along X, 56 along Y, 45 tall, sitting on the plate top (Z 10 to 55), centred at X = -50 and X = +50, Y = 0.\n- Each housing has a horizontal bore along X at (Y = 0, Z = 40) with 0.2 mm radial clearance around the shaft (bore diameter 20.4).\n- shaft: diameter 20, length 140, axis along X at (Y = 0, Z = 40), centred on X = 0.\n- Bolted interface: vertical \u00d89 holes through each housing and through the plate, coaxial, at (X = \u00b150, Y = \u00b120).\n- Parts must touch where they are seated but must not interfere.\nRequired PARAMS keys: plate_length, plate_width, plate_thickness, housing_x, housing_width, housing_depth, housing_height, axis_z, shaft_d, shaft_length, clearance, bolt_d, bolt_dy.",
